From lochapoka at web.de  Wed Sep 15 14:44:56 2004
From: lochapoka at web.de (Volker Bahn)
Date: Wed, 15 Sep 2004 10:44:56 -0400
Subject: Re: Update a variogram to combine terms
References: <OF480B90BC.0CF509FE-ON85256F0F.005F7E82-85256F0F.00612B0F@er.usgs.gov>
Message-ID: <04ae01c49b32$931280f0$c8a66f82@Context>

You can control the bin distances with the arguments lag or maxdist and nlag 
in the function variogram() and the width with tol.lag. However, that does 
not allow you to have bins of different distances within the same variogram 
(i.e., they have to be equally spaced). I'm not sure if arbitrarily spaced 
bins are possible in Splus and advisable in a statistical sense.

HTH

Volker

