Tim Hesterberg

--------------------------------------------------

There are four general sets of S-PLUS bootstrap software available:

(1) The bootstrap, cross-validation, and jackknife functions by 
B. Efron and R. Tibshirani that correspond to their book 
"An Introduction to the Bootstrap" (1993, Chapman and Hall) 
are available from
        http://lib.stat.cmu.edu/S/bootstrap.funs

(2) An extensive set of functions for bootstrapping by Angelo Canty,
which accompany the book:
Bootstrap Methods and Their Application 
by A.C. Davison and D.V. Hinkley (Cambridge University Press, 1997), 
See:
        http://statwww.epfl.ch/davison/BMA/library.html

(3) Versions of S-PLUS 4.0 and later have built-in `bootstrap',
`jackknife', and related functions.  These are easier to use for simple
applications than some of the other sets, but are more limited in scope
and flexibility.

(4) An upgrade to (3) is the S+Resample library, available from
        http://www.insightful.com/downloads/libraries
This offers wide variety of resampling routines.  For further
information see:
        www.insightful.com/Hesterberg/bootstrap

In addition to the packages above, some code for special purposes
is available at
        http://lib.stat.cmu.edu/S
(search for "bootstrap"), including linear regression, nonlinear
heteroskedastic regression, and a weighted likelihood bootstrap.

These are all for the S-PLUS language, for Unix and PC.  Vendor info
